Many there are who flee from one danger to a worse;
Many flee from a snake and meet a dragon. Man plans a stratagem, and thereby snares himself;
What he takes for life turns out to be destruction.

I set my face towards that free grace of Thine;
I have no regard to my own acts.
I set my face towards this hope,
Seeing that Thou gavest me my being first of all;
Thou gavest me the garment of being unasked,
Wherefore I firmly trust in Thy free grace.
